<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alberto Fujimori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a>–<a href="/years/2024">2024</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alberto Fujimori was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from 1990 to 2000. He curbed hyperinflation, closed Congress in a self-coup in 1992 and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shining-path">Shining Path</a> insurgency, whose leader was captured that year. He fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 2000 amid corruption scandals and was later convicted in Peru of human rights abuses and corruption.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alberto-fujimori.jpg" alt="Alberto Fujimori" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Lambiotte / European Communities, 1991 / EC - Audiovisual Service · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Visit_of_Alberto_Fujimori,_President_of_Peru,_to_the_CEC_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Alberto Fujimori</b>, elected in 1990, closed Congress in his self-coup of April 1992 and introduced the 1993 constitution, still in force, which strengthened the presidency and created a single-chamber Congress; a return to two chambers was approved in 2024.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-peru">Republic of Peru · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In France the first president elected by universal male suffrage, Louis-Napoléon Bonaparte, barred from a second term, seized power in a coup in December 1851; in 1992 Peru’s president <b>Alberto Fujimori</b> closed Congress with the army’s support.</blockquote><a href="/government/presidential-democracy">Presidential democracy · Weaknesses</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Miraflores, in what is now <a href="/countries/peru">Peru</a>. Died in San Borja, in what is now <a href="/countries/peru">Peru</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-12.12,-77.03&amp;year=1993" aria-label="Miraflores on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2433 2615 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Alberto Fujimori"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2883 2885h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2883 2885h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-12.12,-77.03&amp;year=1993">What was here in 1993? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
